1
00:02:57,777 --> 00:03:03,777
Hidden by darkness. Guarded by witches. Discovered by a boy. Stolen by a
king. Whoever owns it will rule the world. Or destroy it.

2
00:05:55,555 --> 00:06:01,555
The Black Cauldron is a animation, adventure,
family film directed by Ted Berman.

3
00:08:53,333 --> 00:08:59,333
Taran is an assistant pigkeeper with boyish dreams of becoming a great warrior.

4
00:11:51,111 --> 00:11:57,111
However, he has to put the daydreaming aside when his charge, an oracular pig
named Hen Wen, is kidnapped by an evil lord known as the Horned King.

5
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:54,888
The villain hopes Hen will show him the way to The Black Cauldron, which has
the power to create a giant army of unstoppable soldiers.

6
00:17:46,666 --> 00:17:52,666
Taran (voice), played by Grant Bardsley.

7
00:20:44,444 --> 00:20:50,444
Eilonwy (voice), played by Susan Sheridan.

8
00:23:42,222 --> 00:23:48,222
Gurgi / Doli (voice), played by John Byner.

9
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Fflewddur Fflam (voice), played by Nigel Hawthorne.

10
00:29:37,777 --> 00:29:43,777
The Horned King (voice), played by John Hurt.

11
00:32:35,555 --> 00:32:41,555
Dallben (voice), played by Freddie Jones.

12
00:35:33,333 --> 00:35:39,333
The Black Cauldron is a 1985 American animated dark fantasy
adventure film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation.

13
00:38:31,111 --> 00:38:37,111
It is loosely based on the first two books in The Chronicles of Prydain
series of novels, which are in turn based on Welsh mythology.

14
00:41:28,888 --> 00:41:34,888
The film was directed by Ted Berman and Richard Rich, and features the ensemble voice cast of Grant Bardsley, Susan Sheridan, Freddie Jones,
Nigel Hawthorne, Arthur Malet, John Byner, Phil Fondacaro, and John Hurt, with John Huston serving as the narrator for the prologue.

15
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
Set in the mythical land of Prydain during the Early Middle Ages, the film centers on a wicked emperor known as the Horned
King, who hopes to secure an ancient magical cauldron that will aid him in his desire to conquer the world.

16
00:47:24,444 --> 00:47:30,444
He is opposed by young swineherder Taran, the young Princess Eilonwy, the harp-playing bard Fflewddur Fflam, and a friendly
wild creature named Gurgi, who seek to destroy the cauldron to prevent the Horned King from ruling the world.

17
00:50:22,222 --> 00:50:28,222
Disney acquired the film rights to the books in 1973,
with production beginning in 1980.

18
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
It was originally scheduled to be released at Christmas 1984, but several scenes, particularly in
the film's climax, were found to be disturbing to children during a test screening.

19
00:56:17,777 --> 00:56:23,777
The newly appointed Walt Disney Studios chairman Jeffrey Katzenberg ordered the
scenes to be cut, which caused its release to be delayed to 1985.

20
00:59:15,555 --> 00:59:21,555
It was the first Disney animated film to receive a PG rating, as well as the
first Disney animated film to feature computer-generated imagery.

21
01:02:13,333 --> 01:02:19,333
The Black Cauldron was released by Buena Vista
Pictures Distribution on July 24, 1985.

22
01:05:11,111 --> 01:05:17,111
The film received mixed reviews from critics.

23
01:08:08,888 --> 01:08:14,888
Being the most expensive animated film ever made at the time, it was a box-office bomb, grossing just $21 million
against a budget of $44 million and putting the future of Disney's animation department in jeopardy.

24
01:11:06,666 --> 01:11:12,666
Because of its commercial failure, Disney did not
release the film on home media until 1997.

25
01:14:04,444 --> 01:14:10,444
It has since gained a cult following.

26
01:17:02,222 --> 01:17:08,222
The film explores themes of witch, based on novel or book, pig, magic, sword.
